A headerless file's declaration summary prints a destructuring declaration's pattern whole, a default value's call included: its `(` sits inside the pattern, so the summary doesn't take it for a parameter list and cut the line there, as it cuts `export function load` before its parameters.
== args
input
== file input/options.ts
const { mode = defaultMode(), verbose } = options
export function load(path: string) {}
== stdout
glob view: input
input/options.ts (2 lines): const { mode = defaultMode(), verbose }, export function load
